1. What is normal distribution and uniform distribution?

 Normal Distribution:

 Anything that creates a curve in the form bell or symmetric is called normal distribution.
 Which means data is spread based on the mean
 so in most of the cases, mean median mode will looks similar for the normally distributed data without skewness

 uniform Distribution:

 Anything that is forming a rectangle shape curve or line or plot is called uniform distribution
 as the name indicates, data will be uniformly distributed throughout

2. What is skewness and kurtosis?

This is usually coming during normal distribution.
skewness is the process of finding the data flow on negative or positive skewness.
kurtosis is hte process of finding how bigger the tail is.
smaller the tail is less in outlier and vice versa.

3. What is bernoulli  , binomial and poisson distribution?

Bernoulli ---> Discrete + single output
Binomial ---> Discrete + multiple trail + Positive result (Head or Tail)
Poission ---> Same of the Trail but over the course of certain time interval

4. what is the difference between isnull() and isna() ??

isnull or isna() ---> is to check whether any cell of given data set is empty
isnull().sum() ---> will give count of each of empty cell on column wise
isnull().sum().sum() ---> overall total count null value in the entire dataset

